/-!
# Universal structure selected for authored GSLT-IL

The theorem-level comparison between functional indexed semantics,
double-cell compilation, and proof-relevant relational semantics selects a
layered equipment rather than one global functional category.

* occurrence-bearing authored events freely generate surface paths;
* coherent paths lift exactly to cells indexed by both surface and internal
  commands;
* deterministic elaboration is a typed selection capability, exact precisely
  on covered and determinate profiles;
* Type-valued elaboration additionally separates visible outcome determinacy
  from retained proof-history multiplicity;
* forgetting authored occurrences gives the strict proposition-valued wire
  semantics and is provably non-faithful;
* typed loose routes that earn representation are vertically isomorphic to
  companions of uniquely determined tight maps;
* represented operational routes recover the existing indexed path
  fibration, observation transport, compositional direct execution, and the
  least domain generated by explicitly transported collection capabilities;
* raw ambiguous routes remain meaningful without a global elaboration map.

`SelectedUniversalStructure` packages these laws at their actual scope.  It
does not assert that the current Prime returned-fibre syntax already decodes
every GSLT-IL command; that distinct internal-language question retains its
existing exact-image boundary.
-/

namespace Mettapedia.GSLT.LanguageDef.GSLTIL.UniversalStructure

open Mettapedia.GSLT
open Mettapedia.GSLT.Dynamics
